          "snippet": "The Knowledge Argument, prominently formulated by Frank Jackson and influenced by Thomas Nagel, posits that complete physical knowledge does not entail knowledge of phenomenal experience, thereby challenging physicalism. Proponents argue this supports property dualism or non-physical facts, while critics attempt to reconcile the argument with physicalism through concepts like indexical knowledge or two-dimensional frameworks. The debate also addresses the threat of epiphenomenalism for dualist positions."
