          "snippet": "Kurt Gödel advanced foundational results in logic and set theory, notably the incompleteness theorems which refuted Hilbert's program. He supported these mathematical achievements with philosophical commitments to realism and rationalism, viewing abstract entities as existing independently of human definitions. His work also included demonstrating the consistency of specific axioms within Zermelo-Fraenkel systems."
