          "snippet": "Aristotle advances hylomorphism as a mind-independent framework to resolve puzzles about change, positing that matter and form are essential components of substance. He argues for the primacy of form over matter because it accounts for generation, diachronic persistence, and substantiality, ultimately identifying the soul as the form of living organisms."
