          "title": "raptor-subset-on",
          "url": null,
          "score": 0.6845116,
          "snippet": "Aristotle characterizes the soul as the form of the body through his hylomorphic framework, which explains their relationship using matter and form rather than treating them as identical or separate substances. This view is grounded in a four-cause theory of explanation developed to address puzzles regarding change and generation. Furthermore, Aristotle analyzes specific faculties like nutrition by defining capacities according to their objects while rejecting mechanistic accounts of biological processes."
